# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#relationshipType
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#relationshipType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#relationshipType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#relationshipType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#Relationship> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#Relationship> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#relationshipType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#relationshipType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relationship_type string value from the STIX 2.1 SRO (e.g. 'uses', 'mitigates', 'subtechnique-of'). Drawn from the STIX 2.1 open vocabulary; corresponding named individuals are declared as stones:RelationshipTypeVocabulary instances in vocabularies.ttl. A shortcut object property is also asserted: stones:<type_underscored> from source to target." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stones#relationshipType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "relationshipType" .
